pe":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.3 stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.26100 - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - AMD Ryzen 7 5700X 8-Core Processor (16 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\n`AudioStreamPlayer2D `does not seek at all. Tried various ways to do it (calling `seek()` before `play()`, calling `seek()` after `play()`, making a separate function just to seek from the `AudioStreamPlayer2D` node's dedicated script) but nothing works. \nAlso tried to check playback position via `get_playback_position()` and that also shows 0, regardless of what argument is passed to `seek()`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\n@onready var jump_sound = $JumpSound    # can be any sound, I tested with .wav and .mp3\n\nfunc on_jump():\t\n\tjump_sound.seek(0.3)\n        jump_sound.play()  # plays from 0s, not 0.3s\n\tprint(jump_sound.get_playback_position())  # this will print 0, should have printed 0.3\n\tawait get_tree().create_timer(0.6).timeout\n\tjump_sound.stop()\n\n\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nSee above code. ","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"ht